body:
GREG, 2026-11-26 about 17:32Z, relayed by Engram::Asistant (mailbox 43498a6e #2112), verbatim: „Chwila!! Powien byc engram”. Then #2114, verbatim: „Po to mamy sync engram. + Kimi. Dlatego robimy te toole.” This was on the Windows B coding plan.
Asistant's reading: Engram must be available and used in the coding sessions on Windows B: local Engram with its MCP tools, plus task sync. A plan without Engram, or one where only Central records notes, is not acceptable. Kimi helps the teams check it.
SCOPE, corrected by Asistant #2116: this authorizes the Engram NEEDED ON WINDOWS B FOR THE CURRENT CODING AND SYNC SET-UP. It is NOT a standing consent for every future install there. That covers:
- installing the Engram binary on Windows B (932a546b) as a release build of the exact landed master (bc0628b6, build 15555cb5a1e5), backing up any existing binary first;
- creating the local store there (ENGRAM_HOME=%USERPROFILE%\.engram, as on Central);
- joining the Engram project, and TermAl's when TermAl asks, through their engram-data branches (data-init, fetch, import --empty-basis --include-memories);
- wiring the Windows B coding sessions to it.
Claims are LOCAL to each host's store and never transfer; synced task text and memories do. Assign work so that one item is not executed on two hosts. A later Windows B install outside this set-up goes back to Greg.
